'''Venalo Wintz''' was an individual who spent [[time]] in [[Niima Outpost]] on the [[planet]] [[Jakku]].<ref name="TFA">{{Film|VII}}</ref> Thirty [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Battle of Endor]],<ref name="TFAVD">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> the [[First Order]] deserter [[Finn]] ran past Wintz while searching for [[water]] in Niima. Wintz later walked past Finn being knocked to the ground by the [[scavenger]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], who believed (because of the [[astromech droid]] [[BB-8]]) that the deserter was a [[thief]]. Moments later, the First Order [[Escape from Jakku|attacked]] Niima in search of the BB-8, and Rey, Finn and the [[droid]] ran directly past Wintz while fleeing from [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtroopers]]. While at Niima, Wintz wore [[Color|brown]] [[Clothing|robes]] and a mask.<ref name="TFA" />

==Behind the scenes==
Venalo Wintz was played by an uncredited extra in the film [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']], which was released on [[December 18]], [[2015]]. The character did not receive a name in the film,<ref name="TFA" /> but was identified by the [[Star Wars video games|video game]] ''[[Disney Infinity 3.0]]'', which was released in conjunction with the film. In the game he asks players to aid him in testing and upgrading a [[speeder]] he salvaged.<ref name="DI3.0">''[[Disney Infinity 3.0]]''</ref> Despite the game being non-[[canon]], story group member [[Pablo Hidalgo]] confirmed on [[Wikipedia:Twitter|Twitter]] that the names provided by the game for previously unidentified characters, including Wintz, were considered canon.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/749616406245699584|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2016-07-03|quote=@LelalMekha Yeah, same with Infinity.|archivefile=File:PabloHidalgo-LegoName-Twitter.png|nolive=1}} {{C|In response to: "@pablohidalgo <nowiki>youtube.com/watch?v=JwxAeHPLpPg</nowiki> The Lego game identifies a few BG characters from TFA, but are those names canonical?"}}</ref>

